## 🔧 JENKINS

- Open-source **automation server** used for CI/CD (Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment).
- **Jenkinsfile** – defines pipeline as code (Declarative or Scripted syntax).
- Pipeline stages: Checkout → Build → Test → Package → Deploy.
- **Plugins** – extend Jenkins functionality (Git, Docker, Kubernetes, Slack, SonarQube integrations).
- **Master-Agent (Controller-Node) architecture** – master schedules jobs, agents (nodes) execute them, allows distributed builds.
- **Freestyle jobs** vs **Pipeline jobs** – Pipeline is code-based & more flexible/version-controlled.
- Supports **Webhooks** – auto-trigger builds on Git push.
- **Blue Ocean** – modern visual UI for Jenkins pipelines.
- Credentials Manager – securely store secrets/tokens/SSH keys used in pipelines.
- Integrates with Docker (build & push images), Kubernetes (deploy), and cloud providers.
- Supports parallel stages, post-build actions (email notification, artifact archiving).

