## 📊 AWS CLOUDWATCH

- AWS's native **monitoring and observability service**.
- **Metrics** – collects performance data (CPU, Memory, Disk, Network) from AWS resources.
- **CloudWatch Logs** – centralized log collection & storage from EC2, Lambda, ECS, etc.
- **CloudWatch Alarms** – trigger notifications/actions (via SNS) when metric crosses threshold.
- **CloudWatch Events / EventBridge** – rule-based automation, triggers Lambda/other services on specific events.
- **CloudWatch Dashboards** – customizable visual dashboards for metrics.
- **Log Insights** – query language to analyze log data.
- Custom Metrics – push your own application-level metrics using CloudWatch agent/API.
- Used heavily for Auto Scaling triggers (scale based on CPU utilization, etc.).

